cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "HFL Project 02: Adult-child coresidence and emergency savings capacity among adults 50+"
abstract: >-
  An observational analysis, with a documented analysis plan, of the 2025 Survey
  of Household Economics and Decisionmaking examining whether living with an adult child is associated with
  a lower probability of being able to cover a $2,000 emergency expense from
  savings among U.S. adults age 50 and older, paired with an out-of-sample test
  of whether that information improves prediction for individual households.
type: software
